  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>The long shinbone shatters from the impact of the arrowhead, leaving only the thinner fibula to bear your entire weight…which it cannot do, resulting in the fibula snapping as well. The foot and lower half of your lower leg now dangle freely, with shards of bone poking through the skin. An ugly and complicated open fracture like that will ruin anyone’s day!</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> You gain @Condition[Prone], @Condition[Stunned] (3) and @Condition[Bleeding] (1). If you receive Surgery within a week it’ll count as a @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.2iult41Jehz0F1O8]{Broken Bone (Major)} except you automatically fail any test to avoid long-term effects. Otherwise the leg is permanently useless (see under @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.k00PimCWkff11IA0]{Amputated Parts}). Regardless, you contract a @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.kKccDTGzWzSXCBOb]{Festering Wound} due to the open fracture.</p><p>Extraction will be <strong>Challenging (+0)</strong>.</p>"
    },
